From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:43:13 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: G16: Register the GPU as a cooling device

The firmware holds the GPU's die at 110 C, but nothing limits it for the
chassis, which reached 48 C under GPU load while the CPUs are held to
45 C. Register the GPU as a cooling device so a thermal zone can cap it.

Each cooling state lowers the performance-state cap in region C +0x98 by
one state. The firmware rereads the cap by itself, without a control
message, so the driver writes it before its next publication; on the
J713 a cap of 3 drops vkmark's GPU-bound effect2d scene from 5460 to
3260 FPS, and lifting it restores the rate.

So the power allocator governor can share a zone's budget between the
GPU and the CPUs, power at each state is modelled as dynamic power,
frequency times the square of the core voltage, scaled to the device
tree's maximum power. Requested power is that maximum times the share
of time with work in flight.

The cap's meaning and its lack of a control message are from interface
notes by Ibrahim Syed <ibrahim.syed787b@gmail.com>, written from macOS's
GPU driver.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
